   "textLength": 522,
   "text": "Similar to best practices for in-memory Redis, we recommend storing relatively small keys and values in Flex. If possible, avoid large objects (>10 KB).\nDepending on your application's traffic pattern, using large objects might decrease performance, since the entire value is moved from RAM to Flash storage and vice versa.\nFlex databases cannot store keys or values larger than 4 GB in Flash storage",
